From c8e9472a82dafd13b75c8177ff1a2a0c16436415 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corvid <corvid@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:05:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Corvid v1.6: FFmpeg 9 support

- ffmigrate: migrate stored processes to FFmpeg 7 and later (-vsync is
  gone: the global one is dropped, a per output one becomes -fps_mode;
  legacy NVENC presets and rate controls become p1..p7 plus a tuning).
  The new options exist in FFmpeg 6 too, so a rollback keeps working.
  A newer, unknown FFmpeg no longer stops the container.
- skills: parse the -filters (two flags) and -formats (device flag)
  listings of FFmpeg 7 and later; without it no filter and no format was
  found.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UhjysExATCKDyVfUWLA89B
